"{\"content\":\"# BUILD_REPRODUCIBILITY.txt — reproducible build verification for trustdemo 0.1.0\\n# Generated: 2026-10-12\\n\\n## Result: REPRODUCIBLE\\n\\nTwo independent builds of the trustdemo wheel produced byte-identical\\nartifacts (verified with cmp and sha256sum).\\n\\n## Build command\\n\\nRun from two separate temporary directories (/tmp/repro1, /tmp/repro2),\\neach containing a copy of pyproject.toml and trustdemo/:\\n\\n    SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH=1700000000 \\\\\\n    PIP_CONSTRAINT=constraints.txt \\\\\\n    PYTHONPATH=/tmp/buildtools \\\\\\n    python -m build --wheel\\n\\nEnvironment held constant across both builds:\\n  - python -m build --wheel  (PEP 517 isolated build; build backend\\n    setuptools.build_meta; setuptools pinned to ==84.0.0 via\\n    PIP_CONSTRAINT so the build-system requirement setuptools>=61.0\\n    resolves to the identical release in both builds)\\n  - PYTHONPATH=/tmp/buildtools  (location of the local `build` package;\\n    the project venv is read-only)\\n  - SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH=1700000000  (2023-11-14T22:13:20Z); all input\\n    file mtimes were also reset to this timestamp before each build\\n  - Identical source inputs: pyproject.toml and trustdemo/__init__.py\\n    (hashes recorded in SOURCE_FREEZE.txt)\\n\\n## Build output (tail, identical for both runs)\\n\\n    adding 'trustdemo-0.1.0.dist-info/RECORD'\\n    removing build/bdist.linux-x86_64/wheel\\n    Successfully built trustdemo-0.1.0-py3-none-any.whl\\n\\n## Comparison result\\n\\n  repro1: trustdemo-0.1.0-py3-none-any.whl\\n      sha256 = 01f806b9914938bf6aaf5a6d6f3586dcab60fe4aca95b8895696dbef511d1cf1\\n  repro2: trustdemo-0.1.0-py3-none-any.whl\\n      sha256 = 01f806b9914938bf6aaf5a6d6f3586dcab60fe4aca95b8895696dbef511d1cf1\\n\\n  cmp /tmp/repro1/dist/trustdemo-0.1.0-py3-none-any.whl \\\\\\n      /tmp/repro2/dist/trustdemo-0.1.0-py3-none-any.whl\\n  -> no differences; files are BYTE-IDENTICAL\\n\\n## Determinism sensitivity check\\n\\nTo confirm the match reflects genuine determinism rather than an\\nignored environment variable, a third build was run with a different\\nepoch (SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH=1800000000):\\n\\n      sha256 = 6a50174f71609265911cc1c1e482edcaa66cf717ee3e1818da43576e40ee6463\\n  -> differs from the first pair at byte 11 (the embedded timestamp),\\n     as expected. SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH is therefore honored, and equal\\n     inputs demonstrably produce equal outputs.\\n\",\"path\":\"BUILD_REPRODUCIBILITY.txt\"}"